@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nhi-il25-nouns`
IMPORT `nhi-il25-published-figures`
IMPORT `nhi-s14-income`
IMPORT `nhi-s14-fixed-and-benefits`
IMPORT `nhi-s14-month`

-- TESTS for row IL-25. Every expected value was worked out by hand from the Hebrew text BEFORE the
-- module was run; the arithmetic is in the comment above each group, and none was changed to match
-- what the code computed. Month: March 2026 unless a test says otherwise. Figures: the 2026 record
-- (reduced amount 7,703; maximum 51,910; minimum amount 123; pension amounts 237 and 340). The
-- rates are 3.23% on the part up to 7,703 and 5.17% on the rest (s 14(f1), (b), (c)).
--
-- Scenario values, not law: the minimum income of Schedule K in the F2 tests (6,000), and the
-- figures for 2035 and 2036 in the (g2) edge tests, which are the 2026 figures renamed.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no exemption applies` MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS 35
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS FALSE

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)`
`exemptions of a person aged` a MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS a
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS FALSE

`exemption: a housewife` MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS 40
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS FALSE

`exemption: a student or recruit` MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS 20
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS FALSE

`exemption: section 351(7a) or (11)(2c)` MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS 30
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS FALSE

`exemption: an organ donor` MEANS
    `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)` WITH
        `age in whole years at the start of the month` IS 45
        `a housewife within section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a student or recruit exempt under section 351(11)(2a) or (2b) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `exempt under section 351(7a) or (11)(2c) of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `a living organ donor in a month the Minister of Health has set for the donor` IS TRUE

`kind: an employee, the employer liable` MEANS `an employee for whom the employer is liable for National Insurance contributions`
`kind: an employee liable himself` MEANS `an employee who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself because the employer is not`
`kind: self-employed` MEANS `a self-employed person who is liable for National Insurance contributions himself`
`kind: neither` MEANS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor a self-employed person liable for National Insurance contributions himself`
`kind: early pension` MEANS `one who is paid an early pension, a retirement grant or an adjustment allowance`
`kind: nothing payable under (b) to (e1)` MEANS `an insured person for whom nothing is payable under section 14(b) to (e1) or (f1)`

-- The fully specified month.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
      k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER, ex IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      pc IS A `What old-age pension an insured person is paid`
      sp IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)`
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`the full month of` y `and` m `kind` k `income` x `exempt income` ex `minimum` mi `pension` pc `spouse` sp `exemptions` e MEANS
    `A person's month under section 14` WITH
        `year` IS y
        `month` IS m
        `kind` IS k
        `income` IS x
        `income exempt under section 350A(a) of the National Insurance Law` IS ex
        `minimum income for the person under Schedule K` IS mi
        `old-age pension` IS pc
        `the pension is raised by a spouse's supplement or a spouse's pension` IS sp
        `exemptions` IS e

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`a person of kind` k `with income` x MEANS
    `the full month of` 2026 `and` 3 `kind` k `income` x `exempt income` 0 `minimum` NOTHING `pension` `no old-age pension` `spouse` FALSE `exemptions` `no exemption applies`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`an employee paid` x MEANS `a person of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` x

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER, ex IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`a person of kind` k `with income` x `and exempt income` ex MEANS
    `the full month of` 2026 `and` 3 `kind` k `income` x `exempt income` ex `minimum` NOTHING `pension` `no old-age pension` `spouse` FALSE `exemptions` `no exemption applies`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`an employee paid` x `whose minimum income is` mi MEANS
    `the full month of` 2026 `and` 3 `kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `income` x `exempt income` 0 `minimum` (JUST mi) `pension` `no old-age pension` `spouse` FALSE `exemptions` `no exemption applies`

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER
      pc IS A `What old-age pension an insured person is paid`
      sp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`a pensioner of kind` k `with income` x `paid` pc `spouse supplement` sp MEANS
    `the full month of` 2026 `and` 3 `kind` k `income` x `exempt income` 0 `minimum` NOTHING `pension` pc `spouse` sp `exemptions` `no exemption applies`

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER
      e IS A `The facts that decide the exemptions of section 14(g) and (g1)`
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`a person of kind` k `with income` x `and the exemption facts` e MEANS
    `the full month of` 2026 `and` 3 `kind` k `income` x `exempt income` 0 `minimum` NOTHING `pension` `no old-age pension` `spouse` FALSE `exemptions` e

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
      k IS A `A kind of insured person under section 14`
      x IS A NUMBER, ex IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person's month under section 14`
`a person in` y `and` m `of kind` k `with income` x `and exempt income` ex MEANS
    `the full month of` y `and` m `kind` k `income` x `exempt income` ex `minimum` NOTHING `pension` `no old-age pension` `spouse` FALSE `exemptions` `no exemption applies`

-- The figures for the (g2) edge years: the 2026 record renamed (scenario values, not law).
