`the reduced rate applies, reading the benefit` MEANS `the default readings with the benefit read as` `the reduced rate applies up to the reduced amount` `and` `decline where the readings differ`

§§ `The employee, s 14(b)(1) with (f1): 3.23% up to 7,703 and 5.17% above`

-- By hand. 7,703 x 3.23% = 231.09 + 17.7169 = 248.8069.
-- 5,000 x 3.23% = 161.5.
-- 7,704: 248.8069 + 1 x 5.17% = 248.8586.
-- 20,000: 248.8069 + 12,297 x 5.17% (614.85 + 20.9049 = 635.7549) = 884.5618.
-- 51,910 (the maximum): 248.8069 + 44,207 x 5.17% (2,210.35 + 75.1519 = 2,285.5019) = 2,534.3088.
-- The 20,000 and 51,910 figures are the ones the capstone's tests (row IL-07) supply as inputs.
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 5000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 161.5
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 7703) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 248.8069
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 7704) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 248.8586
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 20000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 884.5618
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 51910) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2534.3088

§§ `Who pays`

-- s 14(b)(1): the employer pays and deducts it from the wage; (b)(2), (c): the insured person.
#ASSERT `who is liable to pay the contribution of the kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` EQUALS `the employer, who deducts it from the employee's wage`
#ASSERT `who is liable to pay the contribution of the kind` `kind: an employee liable himself` EQUALS `the insured person`
#ASSERT `who is liable to pay the contribution of the kind` `kind: self-employed` EQUALS `the insured person`
#ASSERT `who is liable to pay the contribution of the kind` `kind: neither` EQUALS `the insured person`

§§ `The employee liable for himself, the self-employed: the same rates`

-- (b)(2) and (c)(1) say 5.17%, and (f1) names the employee liable for himself and the self-employed
-- person: 20,000 -> 884.5618 as above.
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: an employee liable himself` `with income` 20000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 884.5618
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: self-employed` `with income` 20000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 884.5618
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: self-employed` `with income` 5000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 161.5

§§ `One who is neither: 5.17% on all of it, and not less than the minimum amount, s 14(c)(2)`

-- (f1) names an employer, an employee and a self-employed person, not him: 5.17% throughout.
-- 8,558 x 5.17% = 427.9 + 14.5486 = 442.4486. The Institute's January 2026 example for those who are
-- neither (rental income 12,000 less 3,442 exempt = 8,558) prints National Insurance 931.29 + 104.05
-- = 1,035 in total, i.e. 592.8976 of National Insurance (row IL-04) + 442.4486 = 1,035.3462.
-- Minimum amount 123: 1,000 x 5.17% = 51.7 -> 123; 0 -> 123; 2,379 x 5.17% = 118.95 + 4.0443
-- = 122.9943 -> 123; 2,380 x 5.17% = 119 + 4.046 = 123.046.
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 8558) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 442.4486
#ASSERT 592.8976 PLUS `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 8558) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1035.3462
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 1000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 0) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 2379) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 2380) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123.046
-- Not 3.23% on the first 7,703: that would make 5,000 -> 161.5, and the text gives 5.17% x 5,000 = 258.5.
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 5000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 258.5

§§ `Section 14(f): one for whom nothing is payable under (b) to (e1) pays the minimum amount`

#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: nothing payable under (b) to (e1)` `with income` 0) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: nothing payable under (b) to (e1)` `with income` 90000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123

§§ `The ceiling, fork F1`

-- 51,910 is at the maximum: both readings agree, so the default answers 2,534.3088.
-- 51,911: by the cap 2,534.3088; with no cap 248.8069 + 44,208 x 5.17% = 2,285.5019 + 0.0517
-- = 2,534.3605 + ... : 44,208 x 5.17% = 2,285.5536, total 2,534.3605.
-- 60,000: with the cap 2,534.3088; with no cap 248.8069 + 52,297 x 5.17% (2,614.85 + 88.9049
-- = 2,703.7549) = 2,952.5618.
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 51910) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2534.3088
#ASSERT REFUSED `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 51911) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14 does not say whether the maximum income of Schedule K caps the income, and the readings give different contributions above it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 60000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14 does not say whether the maximum income of Schedule K caps the income, and the readings give different contributions above it"
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 60000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the ceiling read as` `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1 caps the income`) EQUALS 2534.3088
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 60000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the ceiling read as` `no maximum caps the income`) EQUALS 2952.5618
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 51911) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the ceiling read as` `no maximum caps the income`) EQUALS 2534.3605
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 51911) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the ceiling read as` `the maximum income of Schedule K item 1 caps the income`) EQUALS 2534.3088

§§ `The minimum income, fork F2`

-- Scenario minimum income 6,000 (not law). An employee paid 5,000: the readings are 5,000 x 3.23%
-- = 161.5 and 6,000 x 3.23% = 193.8. Paid 6,000 (equal) or 7,000: the minimum does not bite:
-- 6,000 x 3.23% = 193.8; 7,000 x 3.23% = 226.1. With no minimum given (NOTHING), the income stands.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 5000 `whose minimum income is` 6000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14 does not say whether the minimum income of Schedule K raises an income below it, and the readings give different contributions"
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 5000 `whose minimum income is` 6000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the minimum income read as` `the income is what the employee is paid`) EQUALS 161.5
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 5000 `whose minimum income is` 6000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the minimum income read as` `the income is raised to the minimum income of Schedule K item 1`) EQUALS 193.8
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 6000 `whose minimum income is` 6000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 193.8
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 7000 `whose minimum income is` 6000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 226.1

§§ `Section 14(g): the exemptions`

-- Under 18: 17 is exempt, 18 is not (884.5618 on 20,000). The exempt pay nothing, not even the
-- minimum amount of (c)(2) or (f).
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `and the exemption facts` (`exemptions of a person aged` 17)) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `and the exemption facts` (`exemptions of a person aged` 18)) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 884.5618
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 0 `and the exemption facts` (`exemptions of a person aged` 17)) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: nothing payable under (b) to (e1)` `with income` 0 `and the exemption facts` `exemption: a housewife`) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `and the exemption facts` `exemption: a student or recruit`) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `and the exemption facts` `exemption: section 351(7a) or (11)(2c)`) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a person of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `and the exemption facts` `exemption: an organ donor`) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0

§§ `Section 14(e): the old-age pensioner pays a fixed amount`

-- (e)(1): the minimum amount, 123. (e)(2) and (3): 237, or 340 where the spouse's supplement or the
-- spouse's pension applies. (e)(4): the (b) to (d) liability of the insured is displaced, so a
-- pensioner who pays himself on 20,000 pays only 237 (kinds other than an employee whose employer is liable).
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 0 `paid` `an old-age pension with an income supplement, or an additional disability benefit (section 14(e)(1))` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 0 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 237
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: neither` `with income` 0 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` TRUE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 340
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: self-employed` `with income` 20000 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 237
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: an employee liable himself` `with income` 20000 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` TRUE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 340
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 0 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 237

§§ `Fork F4: a pensioner who is an employee for whom the employer is liable, with an income`

-- Displaces: 237. Employer's duty stands beside it: 237 + 884.5618 = 1,121.5618. Default: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14(e)(4) frees the insured person from section 14(b), but section 14(b)(1) is the employer's duty, and the readings give different contributions for a pensioner who is an employee with an income"
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the pensioner read as` `section 14(e) displaces section 14(b) to (d): only the fixed amount is payable`) EQUALS 237
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`a pensioner of kind` `kind: an employee, the employer liable` `with income` 20000 `paid` `an old-age pension without an income supplement, or a person whom section 14(e)(3) adds to (e)(2)` `spouse supplement` FALSE) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the pensioner read as` `the employer's duty under section 14(b)(1) stands beside the fixed amount`) EQUALS 1121.5618

§§ `Fork F5: a computed amount of nothing`

-- An employee paid nothing: the readings are 0 (an amount payable, so (f) does not apply) and 123 (no
-- amount payable, so (f) pays the minimum amount). Default: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 0) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14(f) catches an insured person for whom nothing is payable under (b) to (e1), and the text does not say whether a computed amount of nothing is that; the readings give different contributions"
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 0) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with nothing read as` `a computed amount of nothing is an amount payable, so (f) does not apply`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 0) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with nothing read as` `a computed amount of nothing is no amount payable, so (f) applies`) EQUALS 123
-- An income above nothing is not in the fork: 5,000 -> 161.5 under any reading.
#ASSERT `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 5000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with nothing read as` `a computed amount of nothing is no amount payable, so (f) applies`) EQUALS 161.5

