§§ `Section 14(d): a benefit`

-- Maternity allowance of 10,000 and no other income: reduced rate on 7,703 then full: 367.5618 (as
-- above); the full rate throughout: 517. Default: declined where they differ.
-- With a wage of 20,000 in the month and a benefit of 10,000: one reduced amount across the two:
-- tiered(30,000) 1,401.5618 less tiered(20,000) 884.5618 = 517; one each: tiered(10,000) 367.5618.
-- With a wage of 20,000 and a benefit of 1,000: across: 1,000 x 5.17% = 51.7; each: 1,000 x 3.23% = 32.3;
-- flat: 51.7. A benefit the paragraph does not list: declined.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A benefit paid in a month`
`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` a MEANS
    `A benefit paid in a month` WITH
        `year`   IS 2026
        `month`  IS 3
        `kind`   IS `maternity allowance or pregnancy-protection benefit under Chapter 3`
        `amount` IS a

`an unlisted benefit of 5,000` MEANS
    `A benefit paid in a month` WITH
        `year`   IS 2026
        `month`  IS 3
        `kind`   IS `a benefit the paragraph does not list`
        `amount` IS 5000

#ASSERT REFUSED `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 10000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 0 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14(d) says the employer's rates, and the readings of the reduced rate (F3), and of one reduced amount or two where there is also an income (F6), give different contributions"
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 10000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 0 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the reduced rate applies, reading the benefit` EQUALS 367.5618
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 10000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 0 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the benefit read as` `the full rate applies to all of the benefit` `and` `decline where the readings differ`) EQUALS 517
#ASSERT REFUSED `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 10000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 20000 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the reduced rate applies, reading the benefit` BECAUSE "the reduced amount may be used once across a benefit and an income or once for each (F6), and the readings give different contributions"
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 10000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 20000 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the benefit read as` `the reduced rate applies up to the reduced amount` `and` `one reduced amount across the income and the benefit together`) EQUALS 517
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 10000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 20000 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the benefit read as` `the reduced rate applies up to the reduced amount` `and` `one reduced amount for the income and another for the benefit`) EQUALS 367.5618
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 1000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 20000 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the benefit read as` `the reduced rate applies up to the reduced amount` `and` `one reduced amount across the income and the benefit together`) EQUALS 51.7
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 1000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 20000 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the benefit read as` `the reduced rate applies up to the reduced amount` `and` `one reduced amount for the income and another for the benefit`) EQUALS 32.3
#ASSERT `the contribution on a benefit, for` (`a maternity allowance paid in March 2026 of` 1000) `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 20000 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` (`the default readings with the benefit read as` `the full rate applies to all of the benefit` `and` `decline where the readings differ`) EQUALS 51.7
#ASSERT REFUSED `the contribution on a benefit, for` `an unlisted benefit of 5,000` `when the income in the month on which section 14(b) or (c) is also payable is` 0 `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 14(d)(2) does not list this benefit, so section 14(d) imposes nothing on it"

§§ `Agreement with the National Insurance deduction the capstone uses (Schedule J column D, row IL-04)`

-- The employee's National Insurance deduction is 1.04% up to the reduced collection threshold 7,703
-- and 7% above (Schedule J column D, 2026; IL-04); the health contribution has the same breakpoint, so
-- the two together are 1.04 + 3.23 = 4.27% up to 7,703 and 7 + 5.17 = 12.17% above (12.17% is the
-- figure the Institute's page prints for the part above the threshold of one who is neither,
-- NOTES.md section 3). At 7,703: NI 80.1112 + health 248.8069 = 328.9181 = 7,703 x 4.27%
-- (308.12 + 20.7981). At 20,000: NI 80.1112 + 12,297 x 7% (860.79) = 940.9012; health 884.5618;
-- together 1,825.463 = 328.9181 + 12,297 x 12.17% (1,475.64 + 20.9049 = 1,496.5449 -> 1,825.463).
#ASSERT 7703 TIMES 1.04% PLUS `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 7703) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 328.9181
#ASSERT 7703 TIMES 1.04% PLUS (20000 MINUS 7703) TIMES 7% PLUS `the health insurance contribution for` (`an employee paid` 20000) `with` `the figures for 2026` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1825.463
